  "read": "H15 SUPPORTED IN OUTCOME, CORRECTED IN MECHANISM. The baseline does not reproduce (9/21 rows differ). The opening book is NOT the cause: runner.py was committed already fixed, in the same commit as the baseline, and the pre-fix book indexing does not reproduce the stored rows either. The dominant cause is king_shelter_score, added to evaluate() after the baseline by the H23 fix: zeroing it restores 7 of the 9 drifting rows EXACTLY (all the material/L2-* pairs). The 2 rows that do not restore (random vs L3, L2-d1 vs L3) BOTH involve L3, whose input width changed after the baseline (TOTAL_CHANNELS(28) -> BINARY_CHANNELS(24)) along with the grad_ctx chain-rule fix; those are the residual, and they are named rather than absorbed. Consequence: the re-baseline boundary is the evaluator change, not the book change.",
